Z||000000||KRMFiero||03-24-2001||11:19 AM||||question abbout My 85 5 speed SE         What possition should the clutch leaver be in, currently i have about 1 1/4" of throw and about 2 back towards the cylinder, the clutch does not disangage at all, dont know if it sliped on the bolt or something.         do you know how to adjust it at all?<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-24-2001||11:34 AM||||Hey Kyle!<BR>There is no adjustment...<BR>But check your resavour, see if it is full.<BR>If it is, then there could be air in the system, but unlikely...<BR>Have a friend press on the clutch pedal while you watch at the slave cylinder.<BR>You should see the clutch arm move as much as the pedal travels, if it does, you have clutch problems internally.<BR>If it does not, then air is in the system...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
